---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { contactMailto } from '../../utils/contact';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Alce Niang"
  description="Information about this portfolio’s technical data, Google Fonts, and email contact links."
  lang="en"
>
  <Header slot="header" lang="en" currentPath="/en/privacy/" />
  <article class="policy site-container">
    <p class="section-kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-08">October 8, 2026</time></p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who is responsible for this website?</h2>
      <p>This is the portfolio of Alce Niang, based in Dakar, Senegal. For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:niangalce@gmail.com">niangalce@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Technical information and hosting</h2>
      <p>This portfolio is designed to be delivered as static files. The hosting provider actually used may process technical request and log information (such as IP address, user agent, and requested URL) to provide and secure the service, subject to its own terms and privacy policy.</p>
      <p>The portfolio code does not implement user accounts, analytics, advertising, behavioural tracking, or non-essential cookies.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>The website loads fonts from Google Fonts. For this request, your browser contacts Google servers and may share technical information such as your IP address. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Email contact</h2>
      <p>This website does not include a submission form. Contact links open your email application with Alce’s address and a prefilled subject. The portfolio does not receive or store information you choose to include in your email. You remain in control of reviewing and sending the message.</p>
      <p>If you send an email, its contents and contact details are handled by the sender’s and recipient’s email services. You may also copy the displayed address and use it in the email application of your choice.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Links to external services</h2>
      <p>Links to social networks and external platforms open those services only when you choose to follow them. Their own privacy policies apply.</p>
      <p>On the homepage and the TèrangaDigital case study, the browser may also request the public GitHub API to display the repository description, star count, and last-updated date. This request uses no account, key, or cookie and omits the referring page URL; GitHub still receives the technical information needed to handle the request under its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a>. Local content and the repository link remain available if the API is unavailable.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Questions or requests</h2>
      <p>For questions about personal information included in an email you sent, contact Alce at <a href={contactMailto('en')}>niangalce@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <a class="back-link" href={contactMailto('en')}>Contact Alce Niang</a>
  </article>
  <Footer slot="footer" lang="en" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow-width);
    padding-block: var(--space-20);
  }

  .section-kicker {
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
    font: var(--weight-semibold) var(--font-size-xs) var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--font-size-md);
  }

  section p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  section a {
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-10);
    color: var(--color-accent-primary);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }
</style>
